# SP-294 — trim the Docker build context.
#
# The compose build uses `context: .` (repo root) and the Dockerfile ends with
# `COPY . /app`, so without this file the ENTIRE repo is shipped as build
# context. That was ~344MB per build (SP-328), almost all of it `.venv/`
# (~343MB) plus VCS history, Hypothesis/pytest/ruff caches and IDE folders —
# none of which the image needs (dependencies are installed fresh from
# build/requirements.txt).
#
# IMPORTANT — do NOT add `certs/` or `config/` here. They are required at
# runtime:
#   * certs/  — Betfair certificate login reads BF_CRT_FILE/BF_KEY_FILE, which
#               the .env points at ./certs/client-2048.{crt,key} (see
#               .env.example). The container needs these files on disk.
#   * config/ — logic/simpleStategy.py loads ../config/strategy.yaml at runtime.
# Both are .gitignored/tracked respectively but either way must stay in the
# image, so they are deliberately absent from this ignore list.
#
# The host .env is NOT baked into the image — compose injects it via `env_file`
# at run time — so it is excluded here to keep secrets out of the build context
# and image layers.

# --- Virtual environment (the overwhelming bulk of the old context) ---------
.venv/

# --- Version control --------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --- Python caches / compiled artifacts -------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Editor / IDE / tooling config ------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.kiro/

# --- Secrets / local env (provided at run time via compose env_file) --------
.env

# --- Tests, docs and generated/local-only output ----------------------------
tests/
docs/
README.md
charts/
log/
output/*.log
data/
build/run_deck_data/
build/run_deck_job_definition/
build/sql/

# --- OS cruft ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
